  "description": "The track spacing (Stage F2, ARCHITECTURE decision 52): two edges at one level (less than 512 apart in height) keep their centre lines 256 apart in plan (4 m), except between points within 32768 of each other along the track, which are one junction's tracks parting; a refused edge takes no ID and costs nothing, while the nodes built for it stay. Track 100 per 1024 units of edge length, rounded up, three times on a viaduct. e1 runs (1024, 2048) to (9216, 2048), 8192 long. An edge 255 beside it, joined to nothing, is refused (trackTooClose, e1); e2, 256 beside it at y 2304, is built. Between the two, 128 from each, a viaduct at 511 is too close to both, and the lower numbered, e1, is named; at 512, the clearance, it is e3 (8 lengths of 1024, 2400). From n2, the end of e1, the line goes on east as e4 to n11 (11264, 2048) and e5 to (17408, 2048), and e6 branches from n2 1 in 16 north to (17408, 1536), 8208 long (9 lengths of 1024): a turnout at n2 and a node of the line 2048 past it. The branch is 128 off the line at n11 and 256 off it about 4100 along, so it runs within 256 of e5, with which it shares no node, for about 2050; along the track those points are at most about 8200 apart (back to n2 along e6, 2048 along e4, on along e5), so it is a ladder's parting and allowed. e4 starts 128 from the end of the viaduct e3 but 512 below it, and 256 from the end of e2. Lower down, e7 runs (1024, 6144) to (21504, 6144), 20480 long, and e8 turns 200 south from its end to n16 (21504, 6344). An edge from n16 back west to (1024, 6344) would run 200 beside e7 all the way: near its far end, 20480 along it, the way along the track to the point of e7 beside it is 20480 + 200 + 20480 = 41160, beyond 32768, so it is refused (trackTooClose, e7). Ending at (9216, 6344) instead, 12288 long, every point of it is at most 12288 + 200 + 12288 = 24776 along the track from the points of e7 beside it, and the points of e7 near its end at most 24904 (from (9088, 6144)): e9 (12 lengths of 1024). End to end with nothing between: an edge from (21759, 6144), 255 past the end of e7 (and the start of e8) and joined to it by no track, is refused naming e7; from (21760, 6144), 256 past it, it is e10 (3840, 4 lengths of 1024). Removing an edge two others part by is refused while both are there (tracksWouldBeTooClose, naming them): without e8, e9 would be beside e7 with no track between them, and without e4, e6 beside e5. No edge 11 was built. Spent 9400 of 100,000.",
